## 🕒 JavaScript (main.js) References (from W3Schools)
- **Date Object** — https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_dates.asp  
  Gets the system time to display live hours, minutes, and seconds.

- **getHours(), getMinutes(), getSeconds()** — https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/jsref_gethours.asp  
  Extracts current time data for the on-screen clock.

- **padStart()** — https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/jsref_padstart.asp  
  Ensures double-digit formatting for time display.

- **setInterval()** — https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/met_win_setinterval.asp  
  Updates the clock every second.

- **DOMContentLoaded Event** — https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/event_dom_content_loaded.asp  
  Ensures clock updates only after HTML content is loaded.

- **classList.toggle()** — https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/prop_element_classlist.asp  
  Switches between day/night background themes based on hour.

- **textContent** — https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/prop_node_textcontent.asp  
  Updates on-screen text dynamically without reloading the page.

- **matchMedia()** — https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/met_win_matchmedia.asp  
  Checks user settings for reduced motion and adapts animation behavior.

