##  p5.js (sketch.js) References (from Official p5.js Docs)
- **setup()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/setup  
  Runs once to initialize the canvas and environment.

- **draw()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/draw  
  Continuously loops, updating and rendering each frame.

- **createCanvas()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/createCanvas  
  Sets up the drawing surface for the blobs.

- **resizeCanvas()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/resizeCanvas  
  Adjusts the canvas when the browser window resizes.

- **createGraphics()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/createGraphics  
  Creates an offscreen buffer for more efficient blob rendering.

- **loadPixels() / updatePixels()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/loadPixels  
  Accesses and modifies pixel data for the metaball effect.

- **colorMode()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/colorMode  
  Uses HSB mode for smoother color transitions.

- **map()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/map  
  Converts a value range (used for hue drift).

- **sin()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/sin  
  Produces smooth periodic motion for blob floating.

- **random()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/random  
  Adds natural randomness to blob positions and speeds.

- **constrain()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/constrain  
  Keeps values (like alpha or position) within safe limits.

- **image()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/image  
  Draws the offscreen buffer back onto the visible canvas.

- **millis()** — https://p5js.org/reference/#/p5/millis  
  Provides a running timer used for smooth hue shifting.

